From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yan <superwhisz@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 16:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Strip click/hover events from written book pages (force-op
 exploit fix)

Blocks the "force op book" exploit family where a crafted
WrittenBookContent is delivered via creative-mode slot packets with
{@code click_event:run_command} payloads embedded in its Component
pages. When an op opens the book and clicks the rigged link, the
click_event executes its command with the clicker's permissions —
trivially yielding /op as admin.

Sanitizes incoming creative-slot ItemStacks by walking any
WRITTEN_BOOK_CONTENT page Component tree and rebuilding Styles with
clickEvent + hoverEvent cleared. Vanilla server-built books use
Component#literal and never carry these style fields, so legitimate
loot/quest books are untouched.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
index 810b352..fe61b44 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
@@ -3492,6 +3492,8 @@ public class ServerGamePacketListenerImpl extends ServerCommonPacketListenerImpl
         if (this.player.hasInfiniteMaterials()) {
             boolean drop = packet.slotNum() < 0;
             ItemStack itemStack = packet.itemStack();
+            // SourbyCraft - strip click/hover events from written book pages (force-op exploit fix)
+            dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.security.BookSanitizer.sanitize(itemStack);
             if (!itemStack.isItemEnabled(this.player.level().enabledFeatures())) {
                 return;
             }
